{"task_id": "Mbpp/2", "solution": "from typing import Iterable, Any, Set as ResultCollection\n\ndef similar_elements(seq1: Iterable[Any], seq2: Iterable[Any]) -> ResultCollection:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds common elements between two sequences, returning them as a set.\n    Inputs are not modified.\n    \"\"\"\n    s1 = set(seq1)\n    s2 = set(seq2)\n    return s1.intersection(s2)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/9", "solution": "def find_Rotations(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum positive number of rotations required to get the same string.\n    If no such rotation exists (0 < k < len(s)), returns len(s).\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Iterate through possible rotation values k, from 1 up to n-1.\n    for k in range(1, n):\n        # Perform a left-rotation by k positions.\n        rotated_s = s[k:] + s[:k]\n        # If the rotated string is identical to the original, this k is the minimum rotation.\n        if rotated_s == s:\n            return k\n\n    # If no rotation k (0 < k < n) resulted in the original string,\n    # the string is aperiodic, and n rotations are required.\n    return n"}
