{"task_id": "Mbpp/6", "solution": "def differ_At_One_Bit_Pos(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if two integers differ at exactly one bit position.\n    This is true if their XOR sum has exactly one bit set.\n    \"\"\"\n    x = a ^ b\n    if x == 0:\n        return False\n    return (x & (x - 1)) == 0"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "import math\n\ndef validate_input(n) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Raise TypeError if n is not an int.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"is_not_prime: input must be an integer\")\n\ndef check_divisibility(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if n is composite, False if n is prime. Precondition: n >= 2.\"\"\"\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        return True # Even numbers greater than 2 are composite.\n    # Check for odd divisors from 3 up to the square root of n\n    for i in range(3, int(math.isqrt(n)) + 1, 2):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return True\n    return False\n\ndef is_not_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if n is not prime, False if n is prime.\n       Raises TypeError for non-integer inputs, returns True for n <= 1.\"\"\"\n    validate_input(n)\n\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n    if n == 2:\n        return False\n    \n    return check_divisibility(n)"}
