{"task_id": "Mbpp/129", "solution": "def magic_square_test(matrix):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given matrix is a magic square.\n    A magic square is an n x n matrix containing distinct integers from 1 to n^2,\n    where the sum of the numbers in each row, each column, and both main diagonals is the same.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate that the input is a list (representing rows)\n    if not isinstance(matrix, list):\n        return False\n    \n    n = len(matrix)\n\n    # A magic square must have at least n >= 1\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n    \n    # Check if all rows are lists and have the correct length 'n'\n    for row in matrix:\n        if not isinstance(row, list) or len(row) != n:\n            return False\n\n    flat_elements = []\n    for r_idx in range(n):\n        for c_idx in range(n):\n            element = matrix[r_idx][c_idx]\n            # Validate that all elements are integers\n            if not isinstance(element, int):\n                return False\n            flat_elements.append(element)\n\n    # Validate that the matrix contains distinct integers from 1 to n*n\n    expected_elements_set = set(range(1, n * n + 1))\n    if set(flat_elements) != expected_elements_set:\n        return False\n    \n    # Calculate the magic constant for an n x n magic square\n    # The sum of numbers from 1 to n^2 is (n^2 * (n^2 + 1)) / 2.\n    # Each row/column/diagonal sum is this total sum divided by n.\n    magic_constant = n * (n * n + 1) // 2\n\n    # Check row sums\n    for row in matrix:\n        if sum(row) != magic_constant:\n            return False\n\n    # Check column sums\n    for c_idx in range(n):\n        col_sum = 0\n        for r_idx in range(n):\n            col_sum += matrix[r_idx][c_idx]\n        if col_sum != magic_constant:\n            return False\n\n    # Check main diagonal sum (top-left to bottom-right)\n    main_diag_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        main_diag_sum += matrix[i][i]\n    if main_diag_sum != magic_constant:\n        return False\n\n    # Check anti-diagonal sum (top-right to bottom-left)\n    anti_diag_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        anti_diag_sum += matrix[i][n - 1 - i]\n    if anti_diag_sum != magic_constant:\n        return False\n\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/131", "solution": "class InputString:\n    def __init__(self, value: str) -> None:\n        self.value = value\n        self.length = len(value)\n\n    def __len__(self) -> int:\n        return self.length\n\nclass VowelSet:\n    vowels = {\"a\",\"e\",\"i\",\"o\",\"u\",\"A\",\"E\",\"I\",\"O\",\"U\"}\n\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        pass # Vowels are defined as a class attribute.\n\n    def isVowel(self, c: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Returns True if the character c is a vowel.\"\"\"\n        return c in self.vowels\n\nclass OutputString:\n    def __init__(self, value: str) -> None:\n        self.value = value\n\ndef reverse_vowels(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Reverses only the vowels in a given string, excluding 'y'.\"\"\"\n    input_str = InputString(s)\n    vowel_checker = VowelSet()\n\n    vowel_chars = []\n    vowel_indices = []\n\n    for i, char in enumerate(input_str.value):\n        if vowel_checker.isVowel(char):\n            vowel_chars.append(char)\n            vowel_indices.append(i)\n\n    if len(vowel_chars) <= 1:\n        return s\n\n    vowel_chars.reverse()\n    \n    # Convert string to a list of characters for mutable manipulation\n    result_chars = list(input_str.value)\n\n    for i, original_vowel_idx in enumerate(vowel_indices):\n        result_chars[original_vowel_idx] = vowel_chars[i]\n\n    output_str = OutputString(\"\".join(result_chars))\n    return output_str.value"}
