{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "from dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import List\n\n@dataclass\nclass PowerOfTwoTerm:\n    exponent: int\n    value: int  # value == 2 ** exponent\n\n@dataclass\nclass Representation:\n    terms: List[PowerOfTwoTerm]\n    def sum(self) -> int:\n        return sum(term.value for term in self.terms)\n    def isValid(self) -> bool:\n        # A representation is valid if it contains at least one power-of-two term.\n        return bool(self.terms)\n\n@dataclass\nclass FunctionResult:\n    is_representable: bool\n\ndef _validate_input(n) -> None:\n    # Raises TypeError if the input is not an integer.\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be an integer.\")\n\ndef _decompose_bits(n: int) -> Representation:\n    # Precondition: n > 0. Returns a Representation for each set bit in n.\n    terms: List[PowerOfTwoTerm] = []\n    exponent = 0\n    temp_n = n\n    while temp_n > 0:\n        if temp_n & 1:  # Check if the least significant bit is set\n            terms.append(PowerOfTwoTerm(exponent=exponent, value=2**exponent))\n        temp_n >>= 1  # Right shift to check the next bit\n        exponent += 1\n    return Representation(terms)\n\ndef is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(n) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number can be represented as a sum of non-zero powers of 2.\n    Raises TypeError for non-integer inputs; returns False for n <= 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_input(n)\n\n    if n <= 0:\n        return False\n    else:\n        # Per design, any positive integer can be represented as a sum of distinct powers of two (including 2^0).\n        # We decompose bits to fulfill the design component, but for n > 0, it will always yield a non-empty representation.\n        representation = _decompose_bits(n)\n        return representation.isValid()"}
