{"task_id": "Mbpp/278", "solution": "```python\ndef count_first_elements(input_tuple):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts elements before the first tuple element in input_tuple.\n    Raises TypeError if input_tuple is not a tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_tuple, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"input must be a tuple\")\n    counter = 0\n    for element in input_tuple:\n        if isinstance(element, tuple):\n            return counter\n        counter += 1\n    return 0\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/279", "solution": "class InputValidator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates input n for decagonal number calculation.\n    Raises Exception if n is not an integer or n < 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    def validate(self, n: int) -> None:\n        if not isinstance(n, int):\n            raise Exception(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n        if n < 1:\n            raise Exception(\"Input 'n' must be greater than or equal to 1.\")\n\nclass DecagonalNumberFunction:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the decagonal number using the closed-form formula.\n    \"\"\"\n    def compute(self, n: int) -> int:\n        return 4 * n * n - 3 * n\n\nclass DecagonalNumber:\n    \"\"\"\n    Data holder for a decagonal number, storing its index n and computed value.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, n: int, value: int) -> None:\n        self.n = n\n        self.value = value\n\ndef is_num_decagonal(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the nth decagonal number.\n    Validates input n and computes the value using the formula 4*n^2 - 3*n.\n    \"\"\"\n    validator = InputValidator()\n    validator.validate(n)\n\n    service = DecagonalNumberFunction()\n    return service.compute(n)"}
