{"task_id": "Mbpp/282", "solution": "def sub_list(listA: list[int], listB: list[int]) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Compute element-wise subtraction result[i] == listA[i] - listB[i].\n    Includes validation for input types, element types, and equal lengths.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(listA, list) or not isinstance(listB, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"Inputs must be lists.\")\n\n    if len(listA) != len(listB):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input lists must be of equal length.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(listA)):\n        valA = listA[i]\n        valB = listB[i]\n\n        if not isinstance(valA, int) or not isinstance(valB, int):\n            raise ValueError(\"All list elements must be integers.\")\n\n        result.append(valA - valB)\n\n    return result"}
