{"task_id": "Mbpp/410", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple, Any\n\ndef _is_numeric(value: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a value is an instance of int or float.\"\"\"\n    return isinstance(value, (int, float))\n\ndef _filter_numeric(items: List[Any]) -> Tuple[List[float], List[type]]:\n    \"\"\"Filters a list, collecting numeric values and their original types.\"\"\"\n    numeric_values: List[float] = []\n    original_numeric_types: List[type] = []\n    for item in items:\n        if _is_numeric(item):\n            numeric_values.append(float(item))\n            original_numeric_types.append(type(item))\n    return numeric_values, original_numeric_types\n\ndef _coerce_return_type(min_value: float, original_numeric_types: List[type]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Coerces the minimum value based on its mathematical value and original types present.\n    Returns int if the value is an integer and int types were observed; otherwise returns float.\n    \"\"\"\n    if min_value == int(min_value):\n        if int in original_numeric_types:\n            return int(min_value)\n        else:\n            return min_value\n    else:\n        return min_value\n\ndef min_val(items: List[Any]) -> int | float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the minimum numeric value in a heterogeneous list.\n\n    Ignores non-numeric elements, returns int or float based on policy.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(items, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"min_val expects a single list argument\")\n\n    numeric_values, original_types = _filter_numeric(items)\n\n    if not numeric_values:\n        raise ValueError(\"no numeric values found\")\n\n    min_value = min(numeric_values)\n    return _coerce_return_type(min_value, original_types)"}
