{"task_id": "Mbpp/432", "solution": "class NumericInput:\n    \"\"\"A helper class to wrap input values, though its numeric check is not used due to constraints.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value):\n        self.value = value\n\ndef validate_numeric_args(base1, base2, height) -> tuple[float, float, float]:\n    \"\"\"Converts input arguments to float type. Input validation with type checking and exception raising is omitted as per special instructions.\"\"\"\n    return float(base1), float(base2), float(height)\n\nclass Trapezium:\n    \"\"\"Represents a trapezium with two bases and a height.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, base1: float, base2: float, height: float):\n        self.base1 = base1\n        self.base2 = base2\n        self.height = height\n\nclass MedianResult:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates the computed median value.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, value: float):\n        self.value = value\n\nclass MedianCalculator:\n    \"\"\"Provides methods for calculating trapezium properties, specifically the median length.\"\"\"\n    @staticmethod\n    def computeMedian(trapezium: Trapezium) -> MedianResult:\n        \"\"\"Computes the median length of the trapezium.\"\"\"\n        median_value = (trapezium.base1 + trapezium.base2) / 2\n        return MedianResult(median_value)\n\ndef median_trapezium(base1, base2, height):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the median length of a trapezium, which is the average of its two parallel bases.\n    The result is an integer if integral, otherwise a float.\n    \"\"\"\n    v1, v2, v3 = validate_numeric_args(base1, base2, height)\n    \n    trapezium_obj = Trapezium(base1=v1, base2=v2, height=v3)\n    \n    result_obj = MedianCalculator.computeMedian(trapezium_obj)\n    \n    if result_obj.value == int(result_obj.value):\n        return int(result_obj.value)\n    else:\n        return float(result_obj.value)"}
