{"task_id": "Mbpp/808", "solution": "def check_K(tuple_input, k) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given value k is present in the input tuple.\n    Raises TypeError if tuple_input is not a tuple.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(tuple_input, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"tuple_input must be a tuple\")\n    \n    return k in tuple_input"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/809", "solution": "def check_smaller(first: tuple, second: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if each element of the second tuple is strictly smaller than its corresponding element in the first tuple.\n    Raises ValueError if inputs are invalid according to preconditions.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(first, tuple) or not isinstance(second, tuple):\n        raise ValueError(\"Both inputs must be tuples.\")\n\n    if len(first) != len(second):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have equal length.\")\n\n    for f_val, s_val in zip(first, second):\n        if not (isinstance(f_val, (int, float)) and isinstance(s_val, (int, float))):\n            raise ValueError(\"All elements in tuples must be numeric (int or float).\")\n\n        if s_val >= f_val:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
